AF][/dim]Every area and project note lists its direct child projects in one [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]bob-owned `> [!projects]` callout under a `## Projects` heading [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]Bryan owns, rendered by Bob Ledger Tools as a card in the [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]notebook/album family. The `🧩 **Sub-projects:**` bullet under [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]`^prj` is retired, and no reader ever mistakes a parent for [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]finished while it still has open children.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]10[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]6[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202611/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]subprojects_catalog_section.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202611/subprojects_catalog_section.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]bob-cli-ld[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/bobs-org/bob-cli--beads/blob/main/pages/bob-cli-ld/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]PROJECTS region spec and generated-heading guards[/bold #D7AFFF]             [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]catalog-guards[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]catalog-guards: add the PROJECTS RegionSpec and make every generated [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]catalog heading (Notebooks, Albums, Projects) a never-drawer, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]never-section-target heading, fixing the live #notebooks drawer bug.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Rust catalog row grammar and dual-format SUBOPEN reader[/bold #D7AFFF]       [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]subopen-reader-rust[dim] · [dim][/dim]after catalog-guards[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]subopen-reader-rust: add the shared row grammar/parser, read SUBOPEN [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]from the [!projects] callout with legacy-marker fallback in surface.rs, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and publish shared parity vectors.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Plugin dual-format SUBOPEN reader and conversion guard[/bold #D7AFFF]        [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]subopen-reader-plugins[dim] · [dim][/dim]after subopen-reader-rust[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]subopen-reader-plugins: mirror the reader rule in task-status-cycler [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]against the byte-identical vectors, keep nav conversion from copying the[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]callout, and deploy before any writer ships.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Pure sub-project catalog planner and renderer[/bold #D7AFFF]                 [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]catalog-planner[dim] · [dim][/dim]after subopen-reader-rust[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]catalog-planner: compute hosts, membership, row states, cleaned [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]criteria, ordering, and per-host postimages (callout plus legacy-line [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]removal) as a pure, tested planner.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Highlights snapshot renders the projects catalog[/bold #D7AFFF]              [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]highlights-snapshot[dim] · [dim][/dim]after subopen-reader-rust[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]highlights-snapshot: render [!projects] in Highlights PDFs with state [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]chips, omitting the Closed group, while legacy notes keep their masthead[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]row.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]bob projects list -f json report[/bold #D7AFFF]                              [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]projects-list-json[dim] · [dim][/dim]after catalog-planner[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]projects-list-json: add the versioned JSON report (projects, catalogs, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]findings) that the card consumes, plus a human catalog footer.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Guarded projects sync writes the catalog and retires the line[/bold #D7AFFF] [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]catalog-sync-writer[dim] · [dim][/dim]after catalog-planner, subopen-reader-plugins[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]catalog-sync-writer: compose lifecycle and catalog edits per file, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]install them through the host-catalog transaction, delete the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]legacy-line writer, add -f json, dry-run diffs, and a nightly step.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  8 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Capture writes the parent catalog row at birth[/bold #D7AFFF]                [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]catalog-at-birth[dim] · [dim][/dim]after catalog-sync-writer[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]catalog-at-birth: project-note captures stage the parent's catalog row [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]in the same all-or-nothing batch, refusing a damaged parent catalog.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  9 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Bob Ledger Tools projects catalog card[/bold #D7AFFF]                        [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]projects-catalog-card[dim] · [dim][/dim]after projects-list-json, catalog-sync-writer[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]projects-catalog-card: paint [!projects] as a hued card with live chips,[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]a folded Closed group, sync and capture affordances, auto-sync, and e2e [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]screenshots.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  10 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Docs sweep, decision record, and vault preview[/bold #D7AFFF]               [bold black on #87D7FF] sm